  "studentAnswer": {
    "text": "Differentiate both sides with respect to x. Product rule on x²y: 2xy + x²(dy/dx). Then 3y²(dy/dx). So 2xy + x² dy/dx + 3y² dy/dx = 0. Factor: dy/dx (x² + 3y²) = −2xy, so dy/dx = −2xy / (x² + 3y²)."
  },
